course: dictionary
lesson: 14135
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary lists them as 1), 2) and 3). To find the right one, read the sentence and ask which meaning fits. «My toothpaste is minty and fresh.» Here minty means it tastes of mint.
explain: Minty can also mean in perfect condition, like new. This is informal UK slang. «Dad's old bike is still minty, as if nobody has ever ridden it.» The clue is that the bike looks brand new. Check it: does «as good as new» fit? Yes, so this meaning is right.
explain: The third meaning is older UK slang for angry or annoyed. You will hear it less today, so the words around it are your best clue. «Gran went minty when we left the gate open.» Swap in «angry» and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Minty means tasting or smelling of mint, the plant used in sweets, toothpaste and gum.
fact: «Minty fresh breath» means breath that smells of mint.
fact: Mint leaves have a strong smell from the oils inside them.
fact: Informal UK slang: minty can mean in perfect condition, like new.
fact: Older UK slang: minty can mean angry or annoyed.
exercise: «The minty sweets made my tongue tingle.» What does minty mean here? | Sticky and brown | In perfect condition, like new | Angry and annoyed | *Tasting of mint
exercise: «Dad's old bike is minty, as if it was bought yesterday.» What does minty mean here? | Angry and annoyed | Tasting of mint | Covered in mud | *In perfect condition, like new
exercise: Ruby says, «I brush with minty toothpaste every night.» Which meaning fits best? | Very old | *Tasting of mint | Like new | Angry or annoyed
test: «Sam's grandad went minty when the bus was late again.» What does minty mean here? | Very tired | *Angry or annoyed | Tasting of mint | Like new
test: Which sentence uses minty to mean like new? | «Minty fresh breath is nice to have.» | *«My trainers are still minty, I only wore them once.» | «The minty leaves smelled strong in the garden.» | «The minty gum fizzed in my mouth.»
exam: «My sister was minty when I borrowed her jumper without asking.» What does minty mean here? | *Angry or annoyed | In perfect condition, like new | Tasting of mint | Smelling of flowers
